<main id="main"><div class="wrap"><section class="page-head"><div class="eyebrow">About Alex</div><h1>A human connection.<br>A thoughtful perspective.</h1><p class="lead">Alex Orlando is the person behind Alex Orlando Counselling, a developing Calgary-based practice and education space focused on mental health and addictions.</p></section><div class="content-grid"><div class="prose"><h2>Counselling and education,<br>in conversation.</h2><p>AOC is being shaped around a simple intention: to make room for people’s experiences while making mental health and addictions information easier to understand.</p><p>That means approaching difficult questions with curiosity, recognizing the context of a person’s life, and using clear language rather than unnecessary jargon.</p><h3>Rooted in Calgary</h3><p>The practice is being developed in Calgary, Alberta. Confirmed service arrangements and appointment information will be shared here when booking opens.</p><h3>Getting to know your counsellor</h3><p>Qualifications, professional registration, scope of practice, and any supervision arrangements should be clear before you decide to begin. Alex’s full professional profile will be available before appointments open.</p><a class="btn outline" href="/approach/">Explore My Approach ↗</a></div><aside class="side-box"><h3>Finding the right fit</h3><p>You deserve enough information to make an informed choice about who you work with. A consultation is an opportunity to ask questions about the person, the process, and your goals.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Consultation details ↗</a></aside></div></div></main>
